# ~/.config/svim/vn_overrides
# format: AppName delay_ms strategy
# strategy: backspace | select  (delay_ms ignored when strategy=select)
#
# Uncomment and edit for an app that still drops/reorders characters at the
# default 5ms + backspace strategy:
#
# Ghostty 15 backspace
# Visual Studio Code 0 select
#
# `select` sends Shift+Left to highlight the characters being corrected,
# then types over the selection -- this only works in apps with a real text
# field that treats a keyboard-driven selection as replaceable (confirmed
# working in that kind of app). Terminal emulators (Ghostty, iTerm2,
# Terminal.app, ...) generally do not support keyboard-driven selection at
# all -- Shift+Left just moves the cursor -- so `select` corrupts text
# there instead of fixing it (confirmed empirically). Use `backspace` for
# any terminal app; only reach for `select` on GUI editors/IDEs.
